    <flowData>
      <intermediateExchange id="76293369-b079-53e4-b60d-98b58da4ee35" amount="1.0" unitId="0ffcf2f0-31e5-53bd-b882-80dc6c9c369a" unitContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" activityLinkId="ab469d43-b1f2-5da7-8e00-74a48f103676" intermediateExchangeId="2827ab0a-e3d6-552c-b0d4-8530efac5f72" activityLinkContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" intermediateExchangeContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
        <name xml:lang="en">Paper, recycling, average, at plant</name>
        <unitName xml:lang="en">kilogram</unitName>
        <comment xml:lang="en">Full flow name: Paper, recycling, average, at plant
This module refers to the European recycling paper production based on confidential primary data from 9 common recycling paper (weighted average) on behalf of a project funded by the Swiss Federal Office for the Environment FOEN:  The total annual production is 1'242'000 metric tons which represents about 10.4% of the annual production of the graphical recycling papers (without newspaper) used in the EU. 

This module includes the production of recycled paper in Europe - including waste paper, deinking of pulp, paper production, energy production on-site, internal waste water treatment and transports of the auxiliaries to the paper mill. Not included are the infrastructure and the transport of waste paper to the mill, as this is already included in the used waste paper datasets. 

BAFU mapping audit: {"bafu source exchange index": 0}</comment>
        <outputGroup>0</outputGroup>
      </intermediateExchange>
